A||||51||Nashco||Northstar PROM chip with engine management only!||||10||
Z||000000||Nashco||12-03-2001||11:57 PM||||I'm not sure how many people know this is out there, but I'm new to this and I HAVE to obtain it!<P>A forum member pointed me to a person who has a PROM in his N* that has the engine management software only.  This means that it doesn't require any extra features.  It has full diagnostic capabilities, check engine light works properly, emissions works properly, and it learns the idle as it should.  This is the chip that is in dire need for swapping a N* into a manual transmission equipped car.<P>The PROM does have some minor changes to the fuel and ignition curves to get some reported improvements, but that is unimportant to me at this point.<P>I asked the owner of this chip if he has the .bin file, or if he has the ability to copy it, which he replied that he can do neither.  He states:<P>"I cannot read the PROM.  How would we copy it?  I would want to know for absolute certain that whoever is going to read it knows the pinouts."<P>Ok, step one, who can read a N* PROM with their current setup?  I know there are/have been a few forum members with this ability, but I can't recall who they are and don't want to volunteer those I do recall anyhow.<P>I also asked if he would be interested in sharing this priceless PROM that he has with the rest of the Fiero community, to which he replied:<P>"Possibly.  Howeer, I've got a lot of time and money invested in it.  I'll have to think on this."<P>Now, I understand he has a valuable PROM, but how valuable?  I was thinking perhaps some of us could pay him a certain amount of money he thinks his time is worth, and the chip would become public material.  That way he could "share" the information he has and make it worth his while, but at the same time, we will be contributing to make this general knowledge and obtainable by all.<P>What do you guys/gals have to say about this?<P>Personally, I'm in love with the N* swap, and with this PROM, it is <B>entirely</B> possible to have a near-bolt-in swap.  There are a few minor gremlins, but for the most part, this solves our problems with hooking the N* up to a Getrag.<P>I know there are a few people in the middle of swaps, and also a few who are very seriously consider engine swaps.  This seems like a great time for us all to jump on a bandwagon and try to heave-ho this idea through.  Many people battled with the N* prom in my early days on the forum trying to figure it out, and all have ended up going to Aurora computers, or custom ECMs as far as I know.<P>I'd love if somebody could help direct me or express their interest. <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>Bryce<BR>88 GT||||reg||10
Z||000001||AgaricX||12-04-2001||02:43 AM||||I would purchase a BURNED PROM.  I wouldnt want to go through the mess of trying to burn one myself.  I'm a computer gook, but I really dont know much about automotive computers yet.  Would this just replace a PROM that is in the stock N* Computer... Like installing PROMS to fool the computer's O2 sensors?<P>I have an option to do a N* conversion in the next year, and I abhor automatic trannys.  This would be a must for me.  Or at least better than buting a $1300 aftermarket CPU.<P>Let us all know what develops.<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.agaric.net/fiero/AgaricX.jpg">  <BR>'85 SE 3800SC 5 Spd<BR>I WANT A FASTBACK!!!||||reg||1
Z||000002||Nashco||12-04-2001||09:29 AM||||Installing PROM to fool the O2 sensor?  Not quite...usually you replace the PROM with upgrades to tune a modded car and adjust for different fuel and ignition curves, along with other stuff.<P>This will be a direct plug in; pull the old chip(s) out and pop the new one(s) in.<P>I don't have a chip burner, but if I can get my hands on the .bin file I would buy one.  Anybody with a chip reader can read the PROM, but I don't have a chip reader.  terryk told me which chip it was, but I forgot to write it down...DOH!<P>Does anybody have access to a chip reader for this chip, and would be willing to help out?<P>Bryce<BR>88 GT||||reg||1
Z||000003||Formula88||12-04-2001||09:42 AM||||Correct me if I'm wrong, the the N* ECM doesn't have a removeable "chip".  It has to be reprogrammed rather than have the chip swapped out.  Hypertech makes PowerProgrammers for late model F-bodies, etc. that do this, since they don't have replaceable chips.||||reg||5
Z||000004||Slammed Fiero||12-04-2001||01:40 PM||||I know the guy you speak of Nashco. HE got the Prom from a guy at GM , it was used to test engines on the stand. The guy at GM was going to sell the proms , but actually won the michigan lottery and has no real need for extra cash flow.<P>The owner of the chip was thinking of having it burned , but at no profit to him , so he is leaving it alone for the time beign I believe<P>He raced a Viper with his Getrag Northstar , didn't win , but said it was a good race. I believe after about 60mph the viper pulled away from him.. So you can guesstimate high 4's to 60mph.<BR> I talked to the ownwer of the getrag N* car through email a few times , he said it took a lot of persistance to ge tthe car running right. Far more involved than a Auto tranny N* swap<P><BR><P>------------------<BR>Jonathan McCreery<BR>86 GT 4spd<BR>Koni's , Coilovers, Big Bars , 17" Trmotorsports Typhoons , 11.25" vented discs, Wilwood 4 Piston Calipers , Pirelli P Zero's, Short Shift, No cat , Cold air induction , Geni Stainless tips, White face gauges , Momo shift , momo pedals, Big Bore TB, 70Hp Shot of NOS Autocrossed , Tracked , Dragged? (soon) abused.||||reg||1
Z||000005||Nashco||12-04-2001||02:04 PM||||Hmm, I don't know if this is the same guy, but the history would be cool.  Either way, this chip would be ideal for a N* swap, IMO, because you wouldn't need the extra weight of the Cadillac auto tranny.<P>The guy I talked to did say he had to tweak the fuel and ignition settings on the chip to get it to run good, but it is now a completely ready to go PROM.  I am hoping somebody here would be able to have EXACT instructions of what it takes to copy the PROM, so the owner is comfortable getting them.<P>Anybody wanna help a learning rookie out?  I know it's easy to copy and burn the prom, but I don't know what chip # it uses.  If I can get the chip style (mfg. if necessary) I could research it and find a source and reader/burner for it.<P>Thanks in advance,<P>Bryce<BR>88 GT||||reg||1
