Z||000048||wcapman||12-14-2001||05:58 PM||||I suggest a separate thread for Holley 950 conversions.<BR> However, to answer a few questions, the 950 has a sensor input for an amplified and filtered knock sensor.  This means that you must have something besides just the stock knock sensor.  From what I have been able to tell, the knock sensor could be tuned for any frequency from 6k to 15k  and it makes a big deal.<P>I talked to MSD and their knock sensor is a read out only.  It won't trigger anything.  maybe it could be jiggled a little.... sure wish we could find something out there.  According to Holley, the input needs be be in the 1v range to trigger the electronics.  I could design a little notch filter and op-amp circuit to work with the existing sensor if we can't find something else.<P>I have a friend who works for Holley.  he got me the 950 + wiring harness for employee cost.  Won't tell you what that was but it's real cheap.  When I bought the cams from Alan he programmed the 950.  Seems that the firmware must be changed because the N*DIS is reading 76 deg ahead of a standard engine.  Alan charged me $100 for that when I bought $800 worth of cams and sprockets, etc.  In other words, don't try this at home.  In talking to Alan he seems to have really worked out a lot of the problems and I think he deserves to be paid for them.  Can't wait to get the cams in.<P>I am currently developing a wiring diagram.  There will be a mini fuse block in the computer compartment along with a relay box with 6 relays in it.  I think Holley has it oversimplifed.  Also the standard LT1 wiring harness would be a nasty looking mess on a N*, so I bought all new wiring shells and terminasl from Holley and plan to neaten it up quite a bit.||||reg||1
Z||000049||Will||12-18-2001||10:13 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by wcapman:<BR><B><BR>BTW  Will has been for a short ride in the car.  What were your impressions?  The chip got a problem?<P></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Impressions? FAST!(!!) Faster than a friend's 2000 Camaro SS, at least in the lower gears.<BR>For the short time I was in it, it ran perfectly well. The shift linkage needs a little work, though  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000050||Jay||12-18-2001||01:09 PM||||Will, can you give us the code on the Aurora eprom or the year Aurora that you are using?  I want to try this before I turn over the car.||||reg||1
